# Files Vercel should not upload — and, for anything under api/, must not upload.
#
# ## The build failure this fixes
#
# Vercel turns every non-underscore-prefixed file under `api/` into its own
# Serverless Function. That included the unit tests: `api/guard.test.js`,
# `api/admin.test.js` and five others were each being deployed as a live
# endpoint. They did nothing useful there — a test file exports no handler — but
# they counted, and the Hobby plan allows twelve functions per deployment.
#
# With six real endpoints and six test files the count sat at exactly twelve, so
# the limit was invisible right up until a seventh test file was added and the
# deployment failed with "No more than 12 Serverless Functions can be added to a
# Deployment on the Hobby plan". The functions themselves were fine; the build
# never got far enough to say so.
#
# Excluding them takes the real count to seven and leaves headroom. Nothing is
# lost: tests run in CI via `npm run verify`, which executes them with the Node
# test runner on GitHub Actions and never involves Vercel.
#
# Note that `api/_*.js` files are already excluded by Vercel's own underscore
# convention — that is why `_guard.js`, `_adapters.js` and the rest never counted
# against the limit and why they carry the prefix.
api/*.test.js

# Local test/build output, never needed by a deployment.
node_modules
dist
coverage
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
